{"indicator":"informal","unit":"%","years":[2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"latestWithin":5,"notes":{"COG":"2009 年的調查只涵蓋都市地區。","ARG":"2008–2025 年的調查只涵蓋主要城市或都會區。","PSE":"2024–2025 年的調查不含加薩走廊。","ZAF":"ILOSTAT 2025 年的值是 42.3%（2024 年 34.8%），但農業的非正式比例從 35% 跳到 76%，還多了一類「無法分類」的行業，看起來是處理方式改了，所以不收 2025 年。","TWN":"台灣沒有 ILO 口徑的非正式就業統計（看雇主是否登記、有沒有勞健保等社會保險與帶薪假），所以留空。最接近的是主計總處人力運用調查的「非典型就業」（部分時間、臨時性或人力派遣）：115 年 5 月 79.3 萬人、占全體就業者 6.82%，是 102 年以來最低（115 年人力運用調查，2026-10-23 發布）。非典型看的是工時與契約期間，跟非正式就業的概念不同，只列在這裡對照。"},"notesEn":{"COG":"The survey for 2009 covers urban areas only.","ARG":"The survey for 2008–2025 covers main cities or metropolitan areas only.","PSE":"The survey for 2024–2025 excludes the Gaza Strip.","ZAF":"ILOSTAT's 2025 figure is 42.3% (34.8% in 2024), but the informal share in agriculture jumps from 35% to 76% and a new 'not classified' industry appears, which points to a processing change, so 2025 is left out.","TWN":"Taiwan has no statistics on informal employment in the ILO sense (based on whether the employer is registered and whether the job carries social insurance and paid leave), so it is left blank. The closest figure is 'atypical employment' (part-time, temporary or agency work) in DGBAS's Manpower Utilization Survey: 793,000 people or 6.82% of the employed in May 2026, the lowest since 2013 (2026 survey, published 23 October 2026). Atypical work is about hours and contract length, a different concept from informality, so it is given here for reference only."},"encoding":"delta","aggregates":{"WLD":[-1,592,-3,2,-3,-3,-3,-3,-2,-3,-3,0,-3,0,2,6,-1,1,2,1]},"values":{"AFG":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,861,null,null,null,null],"AGO":[-1,null,null,null,null,843,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,38,10,3,27,31,1,-8],"ARE":[0,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,4],"ARG":[-1,null,511,-6,-12,-8,0,-5,-6,null,